            </profile>
            <profile id="f650-c161-0d18-9bdc" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="37b4-aae5-6830-d590" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">The "poor bloody infantry" of a Roman army. Large shield, sword and throwing spear. May have light armour (+2), javelins and darts (+2), heavy throwing spear instead of throwing spear (+1). May be drilled (+1 pt). Can form shield wall. Archers would normally be deployed at the rear of the unit. One soldier in four may replace the throwing spear and shield with a bow (+1 pt) but may not take other weapon options except light armour (not modelled: all models of a unit are equipped alike). Skirmishers replace their equipment with shield, hand weapon, javelins and darts and may take no other options. One unit may skirmish. (Fall of the West p.46)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="79f9-1de2-7f31-c9f7" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">5+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
