  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="41e4-aa32-e7c0-f61a" name="Warlord (Fall of the West) - List Notes" publicationId="37b4-aae5-6830-d590" hidden="false">
      <description>WARLORD ARMY LIST (Fall of the West, pp.44-48). Any Roman or Barbarian troops may be mixed. A Warlord army may be led by a Roman Army General or a Barbarian Warlord (not both).

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[Warlord Army]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Warlord armies: characters up to 33%, infantry (any) at least 33%, cavalry (any) up to 50%. During the 5th century the distinction between Roman and Barbarian armies broke down; a warlord's army could contain almost any mix of troops.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
